rane  immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells     These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by  the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not  been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The  FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this  laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision            Electronically Signed Out By  Elena F  Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 16 46      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH Quantitation Analyisis    FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION    Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified    See note     Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  154  to  chromosome 17 signals  143  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than  2 0 or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for  chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis     The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be  interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification    Reference  Journal of Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID             Electronically Signed Out By  Elena F  Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 16 57       CLINICAL HISTORY  67 year old female with right breast cancer     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  BREAST  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RIGHT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN    right breast  mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 9 5cm distorted mastectomy specimen  with a REMOVED_DATE  x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm nodular and distorted axillary tail  The specimen is partially  surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 14 5cm portion of ulcerated  nodular pink red and  tan white skin  No definitive nipple areolar complex is identified  The  posterior margin is remarkable for a 