Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  WILLIAM  JAY  G AUSTEN  JR  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Matthew M Johnson  M D  Frozen Section Consultant s   Melinda J Lerwill  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Elizabeth Demicco  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Dennis Sgroi  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer  multifocal on MRI  Right MRI abnormal  Bilateral mastectomy with sentinel node biopsy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA   SEE TABLE  1   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE TABLE  1   3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  invasive  The largest mass displays both invasive ductal and invasive lobular histomorphological and immunoreactivity  e cadherin  features  while the smaller  1 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7  mass displays histomorphological and immunoreactive  e cadherin negative  features of invasive lobular carcinoma  The tissue between the two masses displays invasive lobular carcinoma  Thus  taken together these masses may represent a collision of invasive lobular carcinoma with invasive ductal carcinoma  Immunostains for e cadherin support the above interpretation  GRADE  2  for both masses  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive lobular carcinoma extends to   0 1cm from the anterior margin of the specimen in one focus and to 0 2cm from the anterior margin in a second focus  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   invasive ductal carcinoma  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   invasive lobular carcinoma   LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO ONE OF TWO LYMPH NODES   SEE TABLE  2   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA CONTENTS   DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 13 LYMPH NODES   SEE TABLE  2   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2 SUMMARY OF LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  2  TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  15  including sentinel nodes   Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   2  Extracapsular extension  Slight   in several foci  Other forms of axillary involvement  Soft tissue metastasis  single microscopic focus   0 1cm in slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PRESENT ADJACENT TO AND AWAY FROM THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE   SEE TABLE  3   SEE NOTE   2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU    SEE NOTE   3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS  4  M NCKEBERG MEDIAL CALCIFIC SCLEROSIS  5  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  REMOTE  NOTE  Immunostains for keratin  p63  myosin and calponin support a diagnosis of ductal carcinoma in situ  Immunostain for E cadherin supports a diagnosis of lobular neoplasia  lobular carcinoma in situ   TABLE OF PATHOLO