 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to  0 1cm from the posterior margin of the specimen in one focus  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block 5  NOTE  The two invasive carcinomas demonstrate distinct histomorphological patterns  The larger carcinoma is associated with abundant extracellular mucin while the smaller invasive carcinoma demonstrates distinct neuroendocrine differentiation  as indicated by chromogranin staining  These two tumors may represent multicentric disease  Immunostain for p63  keratin  myosin and calponin support a diagnosis of invasive carcinoma  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE IS FREE OF CARCINOMA   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  SOFT TISSUE  RIGHT BREAST AXILLARY TISSUE   FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE  NO LYMPH NODES ARE IDENTIFIED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Nestor  REMOVE_MRN and  right sentinel lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm tan pink lymph node which is entirely submitted for Frozen Section as FX  1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x 5 7cm portion of tan red fibrofatty tissue partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm tan pink skin ellipse  There is a localization wire in place  The skin displays a 2 5cm tan pink areola with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm depressed tan pink nipple which comes to 1 0cm of the medial margin  A short black stitch designates the superior margin and a long black stitch designates the lateral margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior margin is inked blue  the superior margin is inked green and the inferior margin is inked yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm cavitated mass the center of which contains soft tan to dark red mucoid material  The mass comes to 0 8cm of the posterior margin  1 5cm of the inferior margin  1 8cm of the superior margin  1 5cm of the anterior margin  and  2 0cm of the medial and lateral margins  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm poorly delineated indurated white pink nodule in the mid portion of the specimen which comes to 2 5cm of the cavity end  which abuts the posterior margin  This area is  2 0cm of all additional margins  Representative sections are submitted from lateral to medial as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the lateral end margin en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the medial end margin en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the cavity to closest margins as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the firm nodule entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unoriented portion of tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue  inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a grossly unremarkable tan yellow lobulated cut surface  No discrete mass or lesion is noted  The entire specimen is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REAS