Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Davis  Tracy L  Reports To  MICHELE A GADD  M D  KATHRYN EVE CUNNINGHAM  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID b REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Preop chemotherapy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  SMALL FIBROUS SCAR IN THE REGION OF THE LOCALIZATION CLIP   SEE NOTE   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  ASSOCIATED WITH CALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  The entire specimen was submitted and microscopically examined  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  FOCAL VIABLE METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 21 LYMPH NODES   SEE NOTE   NECROSIS  HISTIOCYTIC INFLAMMATION AND CALCIFICATION  NOTE  The history of preoperative chemotherapy is noted  A matted  nodular aggregate of tissue shows marked fibrohistiocytic inflammation surrounding areas of necrosis with dystrophic calcification  Underlying lymph node architecture is not evident in most areas  One recognizable node within this matted tissue shows viable metastatic carcinoma spanning 0 15cm  without evidence of extracapsular extension  While the other areas of necrosis and inflammation may represent previously involved nodes  the features are not diagnostic due to the absence of cellular detail  Results of studies for ER  PR and Her2neu performed on the focus of viable tumor  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   will be reported in an addendum  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm oval shaped yellow  lobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue  The tissue is oriented with a long stitch designating lateral and a short stitch designating superior  The lateral and superior aspects of the specimen are disrupted  The tissue is inked as follows  superior   blue  inferior   black  medial   green  lateral   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned along the anterior   posterior axis to reveal yellow  lobulated fibroadipose tissue  No masses are identified  The entire specimen is serially submitted from anterior to posterior in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   approximate area of surgical clip  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary content  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm irregular shaped portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned and numerous potential lymph nodes are identified which range in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 3cm  There is a poorly defined area that is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm which is a chalky tan yellow soft tissue area that involves several potential lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four potential lymph nodes involved by described chalky yellow substance   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  quadrisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  bivalved   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  bivalved  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  bivalved  Gross Dictation by Tracy L  Davis  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Tracy L  Davis  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Tracy L  Davis  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Lymph Node  Rig