st   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left radical modified mastectomy specimen with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The anterior surface contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm tan brown skin ellipse which contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm nipple which are grossly unremarkable  There is a 6 5cm linear well healed scar present in the upper outer quadrant approximately between 2 00 and 3 o clock 4cm from the areola  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm stellate fibrous area approximately beneath the linear well healed scar on the overlying skin in the upper outer quadrant  4 0cm from overlying anterior inked margin  and 2 4cm from posterior inked margin  The breast parenchyma surrounding the stellate fibrous area contains foci of chalky discoloration  consistent with fat necrosis  and a metallic clip  There are two tan brown  soft to firm  fairly well circumscribed cystic nodules present approximately 4 0cm and 8 0cm medial to the stellate fibrous area in the central and inner quadrant  The first REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan brown cyst in the central quadrant is present 4 0cm from the overlying anterior and 2 3cm from posterior inked margin  The second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan brown cyst in the inner quadrant is present 4 0cm from overlying anterior and 1 8cm from posterior inked margin  The remaining breast parenchyma contains tan yellow lobulated cut surface interspersed with abundant amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue  No additional discrete mass or lesion is noted  Multiple lymph noes dissected ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to 2 x 2 x 0 8cm Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  nodular fibrous breast parenchyma adjac