Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  MS 11  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   CASE  MS 11  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3    Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2  Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D   Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D              Addended Report                Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results  Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH   Results  CLINICAL DATA   Right breast cancer       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE 1 AND NOTE 1    DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  WITH NECROSIS AND CALCIFICATIONS   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES   FIBROADENOMA   HEALING BIOPSY SITE     NOTE 1  Two invasive tumors are identified  one of them in the main  wire localized excision adjacent to the healing biopsy site  and the other  within the final deep margin specimen  The two tumors have different  histological appearances  one of them is grade 2 overall with high grade  nuclei  while the other is grade 1  with low grade nuclei and certain features  of tubular carcinoma  For each of the tumors  the results of  immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and  Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies  for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum       TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   1  RIGHT BREAST INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1    TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  gross measurement    GRADE  2   LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified   BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified   MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to 0 19cm from the  superior margin of the specimen along a broad front   LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the mass   GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA I