d precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 31     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     THE INVASIVE TUMOR IS FOCALLY REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR MARGIN AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE POSTERIOR MARGIN  NOTE  Although the close margin in slides E and F is not inked blue  it is at the junction of the green  anterior  and black  posterior  inks and opposite the yellow  inferior   and therefore is interpreted as superior  Added by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 12 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tumor short superior  long lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with two black stitches designating the superior and lateral margins  The specimen has a localization wire in place  The posterior margin is inked black  anterior green  inferior yellow  and superior blue  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a metal clip surrounded by a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm hemorrhagic focus  The fibrous tissue shows diffuse yellow orange foci and is focally dense with no discrete lesion  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as A F with the hemorrhagic focus as D F and the area designated by the clip and localization wire as F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary lymph node stitch at highest lymph node  is a 11 x 8 x 3 0cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a black stitch at one end designated as highest lymph node as per requisition  The specimen is divided into levels high  mid and low  Sectioning of the highest level reveals seven tan red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 9cm in greatest dimension  Sectioning of the mid level reveals eleven tan red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  Sectioning of the lowest lev