Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 03 CLINICAL DATA  60 year old female with a history of breast cancer of the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WITH FEATURES OF BOTH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA WITH FOCAL SIGNET RING CELLS EXTENDING TO AN INKED RESECTION SURFACE  SEE NOTE  1  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  FAT NECROSIS  FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  AND FIBROSIS CONSISTENT WITH HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  1  Several foci suspicious of but not diagnostic of lymphatic invasion are present  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  METASTATIC MAMMARY CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 19 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  2  NOTE  2  The focus measures less than 0 2cm and does not extend beyond the lymph node capsule  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 07 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in two separate parts  Labeled  right breast mass  is a 52 gram  unoriented  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast lumpectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm skin ellipse  containing a 4 2cm long  centrally located  well healed scar  The breast tissue is very fragmented and the borders are very ragged and irregular  The entire specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm cystic cavity that is lined by tan  smooth  focally hemorrhagic epithelium and is surrounded by soft bright yellow to tan  firm  focally hemorrhagic tissue that extends to the deep  as well as another inked resection margin  The cystic cavity lies 1 7cm deep the skin ellipse  and lies focally at the deep  as well as one other inked resection margin  Apart from the biopsy cavity  a 1 0cm in diameter  white  shiny  firm area with irregular and ill defined borders approaches the deep inked resection margin  The remaining parenchyma is yellow  soft  and lobulated  SECTION CODE  A  skin with scar and biopsy cavity B D  biopsy cavity with closest inked resection  deep and side  E F  biopsy cavity  representative sections G H  firm area  entirely I  breast  representative section  Labeled  axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is dissected to reveal multiple  19  lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 9cm in greatest dimension  with tan to fatty cut surfaces  Submitted in J through O  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  AXILLARY NODES  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
