Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 11 17 CLINICAL DATA  62 year old female with history of ovarian serous carcinoma in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   with an approximately 3cm mass in the left breast  Lumpectomy and sentinel node biopsy performed  Final shaving at tumor margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODES  LEFT SENTINEL   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 NODES  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NO TUMOR CELLS ARE IDENTIFIED BY KERATIN IMMUNOSTAINS ON THREE LEVELS OF THIS TISSUE BLOCK  LYMPH NODE  LEFT SENTINEL  LOWER AXILLA   BIOPSY  METASTASTIC CARCINOMA  ONE NODE   OCCASIONAL CLUSTERS IN SUBCAPSULAR SINUS  CONFIRMED BY IMMUNOSTAINS FOR KERATIN  WITHOUT EXTRANODAL EXTENSION  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Tumor cells are not present on the frozen section slide  but are present on a fixed tissue slide and on immunostains  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  GROSS MEASUREMENT   POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION  AND SATELLITE FOCI  ONE OF WHICH IS PRESENT AT A MEDIAL MARGIN  H   SEE NOTE  FAT NECROSIS  CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR CORE BIOPSY  NOTE  The tumor is similar enough histologically to the previous ovarian carcinoma last diagnosed in  REMOVED_CASE_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   to suggest that the present tumor may be a metastasis from the ovary  Supporting this is multifocality  extensive lymphatic invasion  and the lack of a definite in situ component  Immunostains are negative for gross cystic disease fluid protein 15  CA 125 and CA 19 9  and focally positive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID protein  findings that are non contributory in making the distinction  A new primary ductal carcinoma must therefore also be considered  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVING  BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 16 27 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fatty tissue containing two lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  One half of each lymph node is frozen as fx 1 and the remainder is frozen as FX 1A  Both frozen tissues are resubmitted in cassette A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left sentinel node lower axilla   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm lymph node with a moderate amount of attached adipose tissue  The lymph node is dissected from the adipose tissue  bisected and entirely frozen as FX 2 and resubmitted in cassette B  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name a