ivity or  incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells     Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete or incomplete  membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells     Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity  in   10  of tumor cells     Reference  ASCO CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing Guideline Update  Arch Pathol Lab Med   doi 10  REMOVED_CASE_ID  arpa  REMOVED_CASE_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  SA             Electronically Signed Out By  Atul K Bhan MBBS  MD on REMOVED_DATE 10 30       HER 2 FISH Quantitation Analysis  Ordered Date  REMOVED_DATE    A  BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  LEFT   Block tested   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified          Note  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates HER 2 neu gene  amplification     Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals to chromosome 17    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   signals in 30 tumor cell nuclei using PathVysion by HER 2 DNA Probe Kit   Abbott Molecular Inc    The average HER 2 copy number cell is REMOVED_DATE and the  average  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  copy number cell is REMOVED_DATE    Results near the cutoff point  HER 2  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ratio 2 0  should be interpreted with  caution if the HER 2  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ratio is   2 with the average HER 2 copy number equal  to or greater than 4 and   REMOVED_DATE signals per cell  equivocal amplification      Reference  ASCO CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing Guideline Update  Arch Pathol Lab Med   doi 10  REMOVED_CASE_ID  arpa  REMOVED_CASE_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  SA             Electronically Signed Out By  Elena F  Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 16 42       CLINICAL HISTORY  37 year old female with inflammatory breast cancer of the left breast  Status  post pre operative chemotherapy     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME     REMOVED_CASE_ID     left breast  left  modified radical mastectomy  short superior  long lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  5 9cm mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the superior aspect  and long suture designating the lateral aspect  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 10 6cm  tan white skin ellipse is remarkable for a centrally located  mildly retracted  nipple areolar complex  with no additional visible skin changes  The anterior  margin is inked blue and the posterior is inked black  The specimen is serially  sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm stellate  irregular  firm tan white  mass that appears centered subjacent to the nipple and extends throughout most  of the breast  The lateral aspect of the mass is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  4 0cm area of tan white fleshy change containing a ribbon shaped metal clip   An additional potential biopsy site is identified approximately 1 0cm medial to  the metal clip  The mass is located a closest distance of  0 1cm to the black  inked posterior margin  0 3cm to the closest blue inked anterior margin  3 5cm  from the medial most aspect of the specimen  7 0cm from the lateral most aspect  of the specimen  3 5cm to the superior most aspect of the specimen  and 0 3cm  to the inferior most aspect of the specimen  The remaining tissue consists of  fat and dense gray white rubbery fibrous tissue  No additional masses or  lesions are identified  Multiple intact candidate lymph nodes are palpated in  the lateral tissue  The following representative sections are submitted     SECTION CODE    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from lateral fleshy nodule within the large mass   to include area containing the clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and closest black inked posterior  margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of mass  submitted from lateral to  medial  to include possible biopsy site in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   closest blue inked anterior  margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and mass to areolar skin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 intact candidate lymph node  bisected    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 intact candidate lymph nodes each    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Unremarkable breast parenchyma lateral to the mass     Additional sections were subsequently submitted as follows    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of tumor to areolar skin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of mass to lateral  grossly uninvolved skin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 intact candidate lymph nodes    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary fat with potential lymph nodes     Immunohistochemical and in situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts  General Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics  determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of  Pathology at Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or  approved by the U S Food and Drug Administration  FDA   the FDA has determined  that such clearance or approval is not necessary       PART   BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  LEFT       report_end  , Unchecked.
