asuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm  and comes to within 0 3cm of the deep margin  The area around the biopsy cavity consists of unremarkable breast tissue  The margin of the cavity is submitted in cassette K  6 0cm medial to this cavity is a white  fibrous  stellate  puckered firm area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  This lesion comes to within 1 5cm of the nearest excisional margin  Representative sections of the stellate lesion are submitted in cassettes L through O  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  DUCATAL CARCINOMA OF BREAST  IN SITU AND INVASIVE  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 29 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT POSTERIOR LESION   INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED SURGICAL MARGINS WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION IDENTIFIED  BREAST  RIGHT ANTERIOR LESION   INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED SURGICAL MARGINS WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION IDENTIFIED  NOTE  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  James F  XxSouthern Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 49 Proofread by  XXSOUTHERN JAMES F                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  ANTERIOR AND POSTERIOR SPECIMENS   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumo