HOT SPOT  O  CT 295    METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EXTRA NODAL EXTENSION    LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  HOT SPOT  0  CT  186    METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EXTRANODAL EXTENSION    LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  HOT SPOT  0  CT  585    METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EXTRANODAL EXTENSION    LEFT AXILLARY LYMPHADENECTOMY  LEVEL I    METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 5 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  THERE IS NO EXTRANODAL EXTENSION  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  09 AUG 95 at 16 46                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 AUG 95 at 09 42    REVISED REMOVED_DATE    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left chest wall nodule   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 05cm tan yellow piece of tissue  entirely frozen as FX 1  now submitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are nine separate parts  Labeled  left axillary lymphadenectomy  level II   is a 1 0cm soft tissue containing two 0 2cm nodules  submitted entirely in cassette B  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  hot spot  1  ct   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a 1 5cm fatty tissue containing a 1 0cm lymph node and a 0 3cm lymph node  Both lymph nodes are submitted entirely in Cassette C  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  hot spot  1  ct  589   is a 0 6cm lymph node  submitted entirely in cassette D  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  hot spot  1  ct  687   is a 0 6cm lymph node  submitted entirely in cassette E  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  hot spot  0  ct  295   is a 0 5cm lymph node  submitted entirely in cassette F  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  hot spot  0  ct  186   is a 0 6cm lymph node  submitted entirely in cassette G  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  hot spot  0  ct  585   is a 1 0cm lymph node  submitted entirely in cassette H  Labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm breast with a 3 5cm skin ellipse containing a 1 0cm unremarkable nipple  Sectioning revealed a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan  firm area parallel and lateral to the nipple and 1 0cm from the deep surgical margin  This area is also stained with a blue dye  SECTION CODE  I  breast tissue  3 0cm medial to the nipple  J  section  1 5cm medial to the nipple  K  firm area  1 0cm lateral to the nipple including posterior surgical margin  L  section  2 0cm lateral to the nipple including anterior m