Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 45 CLINICAL DATA  Mammographic density                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Lymphatic vessel and blood vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 36 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast with needle localization  are two fragments of tan yellow  fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  with a wire  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  respectively  The fragment containing the wire is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1cm in largest dimension hard stellate mass  with an ill defined border and with fibrous extension to the inked margin  The lesion is fully in A through C  Representative sections of tissue away from the lesion are in D and E  The second fragment is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast tissue  This fragment is entirely in F through J  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  CLOSELY APPROACHING THE MARGIN  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
