ce T  McKee MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 11 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left sentinel node hot and blue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of adipose tissue with lymph node  which is bivalved to show a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node  which frozen entirely as FX  1 and now re submitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast excision   is an oriented fragment of fibrofatty breast parenchyma  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  A single short stitch denotes the superior margin and two stitches denote the lateral margin  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  and superior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm ill defined  gelatinous and blue discolored nodule  The nodule is 0 6cm from the anterior margin  0 6cm from the posterior margin  3 1cm from the superior margin  1 6cm from the inferior margin  2 2cm from the medial margin  and 4 1cm from the lateral margin  The surrounding breast parenchyma is predominantly fibrofatty with a focal firm nodularity of tan white fibrous tissue present at the anterior superior aspect of the specimen  No other distinct masses or lesions are identified  Representative sections are submitted as per cassette code  SECTION CODES  B F  blue discolored lesion  entirely submitted  laterally towards medially   G H  firm tan white region in anterior superior portion of tissue  I   representative section of unremarkable breast parenchyma  Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     LEFT SENTINEL NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCEW OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  MASSIMO D APUZZO  MD PhD O R  Diagnosis by  MANCONG ZHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKN