Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 22 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  65   WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  35   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The infiltrating tumor component extends to within 0 1cm to the inked margin  and the intraductal component is focally less than 0 1cm from the inked margin  The tumor measures 1 2cm in greatest dimension on paraffin embedded tissue  There is no unequivocal evidence of lymphatic or vascular invasion  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  FLORID  3  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 18 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm ovoid piece of fibrofatty breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm tan pink  irregular  firm  nodule with a 0 8cm  ovoid  tan  hard area located adjacent to the inked resection margin  Representative sections of the hard area is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  The remaining tissue is submitted in A through G  Resident  FANG FANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS , Unchecked.
