Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 56 CLINICAL DATA  Status post right lumpectomy  radiation and chemotherapy treatment for infiltrating ductal carcinoma of the right breast in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Now with an  inflammatory  recurrence in the right breast  The patient also has a history of left breast carcinoma in  REMOVED_CASE_ID  with a poorly differentiated infiltrating ductal carcinoma and positive nodes                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The carcinoma is small  approximately 0 4cm in diameter and is embedded in dense scar tissue  An intraductal tumorcomponent is not seen  All resection margins are free of tumor  There is no unequivocal lymphatic or vascular invasion  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 58                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 94 at 07 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast   is a 375 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm simple mastectomy specimen covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm triangular skin ellipse with a centrally placed 0 8cm unremarkable nipple  The breast is oriented with a short suture marking the superior and a long stitch marking the lateral skin ellipse  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan white  firm  irregular stellate mass with a central 1 5cm rock hard  tan area that extends 0 5cm deep and 3 0cm medially to the nipple  The mass extends 0 3cm to the closest deep margin  abuts the inferior margin  and to within 0 5cm from the skin and 2 0cm from the superior margin  There is an adjacent tan white  rubbery  fibrous area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm adjacent to the breast mass extending 2 0cm laterally  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A B  mass with closest deep margin  D E  mass with closest inferior margin  F  mass with adjacent inferior margin  G  overlying skin adjacent to mass  H  more portion of section in cassette G  including deep margin  I  representative sections of superior margin  J  representative section of fibrous areas adjacent to mass  lateral   K  representative sections of adjacent fibrous area with inferior margin  L  skin with adjacent fibrous area  adjacent to nipple  M  nipple  N  representative section of unremarkable breast tissue  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Simon Bergman  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
