l 3 2cm in diameter unremarkable areola containing a 0 7cm in diameter unremarkable nipple  There is a flat elongated portion of tissue that is consistent with a partial axillary tail  This tissue contains no identifiable lymph nodes  however it is used to orient the specimen  The specimen is inked anterior blue and posterior black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm pale golden to focally punctate red firm fibrotic appearing mass consistent with a prior biopsy site  This biopsy site lies in the lower inner quadrant 1cm from the nipple  4cm from the inferior margin  8cm from the superior margin  3 5cm from the posterior margin  2 2cm from the medial margin  and 14cm from the lateral margin  The remaining breast parenchyma consist of unremarkable tan yellow adipose tissue admixed with scant tan white wispy fibrous appearing tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy site with nipple included in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remote tissue from upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remote tissue from lower outer quadrant  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right sentinel node breast  668    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of tan yellow soft tissue that is trisected and entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right sentinel node  174    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of tan pink lymph node within fatty tissue that is bivalved and entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right sentinel node breast  205    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of tan yellow soft tissue that is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation b