Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 36 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    GRADE II III  WITH FOCAL NECROSIS  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AS MEASURED ON A GLASS SLIDE  PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF MARGIN  WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  PRESENT AT INKED SURFACE  PRESENT ADJACENT TO AND AWAY FROM INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  3  PAPILLOMA  MICROSCOPIC  4  CALCIFICATION WITHIN LOBULES ADJACENT TO CARCINOMA  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The intraoperative diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 14                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results o