Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 AUG 95 ACCESSIONED ON  22 AUG 95 at 13 19 CLINICAL DATA    FNA of right breast mass  1cm palpable nodes  Long stitch lateral  short stitch superior                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  ATYPICAL MEDULLARY CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear negative for the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 15 OF 15 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 AUG 95 at 15 37                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The rumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 15 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast and axillary nodes  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of breast and axillary tail  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm skin ellipse overlying the specimen  There is a 1 5cm diameter nipple present on the skin ellipse  The nipple appears unremarkable  1 0cm inferior and 2 0cm lateral to the skin ellipse is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm  focally well circumscribed mass with a tan gritty cut surface  The mass extends to 0 1cm of the deep margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is focally firm and white with areas of fibrofatty tissue  The axillary nodes are as large as 1 5cm in diameter and firm and pink  Section Code  A  mass  deep margin  B  mass  anterior margin  C D  mass  anterior and deep margin  D  mass  E J  representative sections of breast  K R  nodes from axillary tail  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY SPECIMEN   report_end  , Unchecked.
